#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:4
msgid "Step 2: Using CTest Launchers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:6
msgid ""
"This step extends :ref:`Step 1 <CTest Dashboard Step 1>` by enabling CTest "
"launchers, which give more detailed reports of build warnings and errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:9
msgid "Step2/submit.cmake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:9
msgid ""
"set(CTEST_BUILD_NAME \"Step2: launchers\")\n"
"site_name(CTEST_SITE)\n"
"set(CTEST_SOURCE_DIRECTORY \"${CTEST_SCRIPT_DIRECTORY}/../Project\")\n"
"set(CTEST_BINARY_DIRECTORY \"${CTEST_SCRIPT_DIRECTORY}/build\")\n"
"set(CTEST_CMAKE_GENERATOR \"Unix Makefiles\")\n"
"set(CTEST_NOTES_FILES \"${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_FILE}\")\n"
"\n"
"set(CTEST_UPDATE_COMMAND \"git\")\n"
"set(CTEST_UPDATE_VERSION_ONLY 1)\n"
"\n"
"# Enable CTest launchers.  This allows us to capture more granular build\n"
"# warning/error information by wrapping each build command.\n"
"set(CTEST_USE_LAUNCHERS 1)\n"
"\n"
"ctest_empty_binary_directory(\"${CTEST_BINARY_DIRECTORY}\")\n"
"\n"
"ctest_start(Experimental)\n"
"ctest_update()\n"
"\n"
"# Add a target that fails to compile, to show how launchers report it.\n"
"ctest_configure(OPTIONS \"-DDASHBOARD_EXAMPLE_BUILD_ERROR=ON\")\n"
"\n"
"ctest_build()\n"
"ctest_test()\n"
"ctest_submit()\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:13
msgid ""
"When :variable:`CTEST_USE_LAUNCHERS` is enabled, CTest wraps each compile, "
"link, and custom command in a launcher.  If a command produces a warning or "
"error, CTest records its command line, working directory, and output, and "
"includes them in the submission.  Without launchers, CTest only scans the "
"whole build output, which makes it harder to tell which command produced a "
"given message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:20
msgid ""
"To show this, the script configures the project with the "
"``DASHBOARD_EXAMPLE_BUILD_ERROR`` option, which adds a target whose source "
"file calls an undeclared function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:24
msgid "Project/error.cxx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:24
msgid ""
"int main()\n"
"{\n"
"  // This function is not declared, so this file fails to compile.\n"
"  undeclared_function();\n"
"  return 1;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:28
msgid ""
"On CDash, the build shows the compiler command line that failed, the error "
"message, and the source file and line.  This makes triage significantly "
"faster on large projects where a single failing compilation step may be "
"buried in megabytes of build output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:33
msgid ""
"Depending on the build tool, the build may stop at the error before it "
"builds the test executables.  In that case, the ``Test`` step reports that "
"it cannot find them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:37
msgid ""
"Launchers require that the project includes the :module:`CTest` module, and "
"that the project is configured by :command:`ctest_configure` so that CTest "
"can add the launchers to the build system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:42
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:44
msgid ""
"A build tool supporting launchers (the :ref:`Makefile Generators` "
"or :ref:`Ninja Generators`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:48
msgid "Running the Script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/Using CTest Launchers.rst:50
msgid "ctest -S Step2/submit.cmake -V"
msgstr ""
